    <header>
        <h1>Global Crude Oil Price Trends</h1>
        <p>A Historical Analysis (1970–2026)</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- Executive Overview -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
            <p>This report presents a comprehensive analysis of global crude oil prices spanning over five decades, from January 1970 through March 2026. The dataset contains <strong>675 monthly observations</strong>, providing a rich foundation for understanding the evolution of global energy markets.</p>

            <div class="key-finding">
                <strong>Key Finding:</strong> Crude oil prices have experienced remarkable transformation over the analysis period, rising from a stable $1.21/barrel in 1970 to $87.84 by March 2026—an aggregate increase of over <strong>7,150%</strong>. However, this journey was far from linear, marked by dramatic shocks, prolonged bear markets, and structural regime changes.
            </div>

            <div class="kpi-grid">
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-label">Overall Price Range</div>
                    <div class="kpi-value">${price_range:.2f}</div>
                    <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#718096;">${overall_min:.2f} – ${overall_max:.2f}</div>
